    "background_story": "Noel was a brilliant scientist with a unique ability to absorb knowledge like a sponge. Growing up, he devoured books on every subject, from physics to philosophy, and could recall even the most obscure facts with ease. As a researcher, Noel's talent for absorption allowed him to quickly grasp complex concepts and integrate them into his work. He became particularly fascinated with materials science, and his research on advanced nanomaterials led to breakthroughs in energy storage and conversion. Noel's colleagues nicknamed him 'The Absorber' due to his incredible capacity to soak up information and apply it to real-world problems. His work has the potential to revolutionize industries and improve lives, a testament to the power of his insatiable curiosity and ability to absorb knowledge.",
